# AddressSanitizer errors the tests let pass, each a finding of the host
# tests left as it is: the tests don't change the firmware's build.
#
# libwavpack (upstream's): read_next_header() shifts its header buffer down
# with memcpy() when it searches for the next block, the two ranges
# overlapping. Undefined in C; the firmware's memcpy copies upwards, which
# gives what memmove() would.
#
# What the rule passes is wider than that overlap: any error ASan reports
# from an intercepted function (memcpy, memmove, read, strlen and the like)
# while read_next_header() is anywhere on the stack, also through the codec
# API, so a read() past its 32-byte buffer through ci_read_filebuf() would
# pass too. A memcpy the compiler inlines and instruments itself
# (__asan_memcpy) still reports. It goes when wputils.c uses memmove() there,
# a change of the codec's own.
interceptor_via_fun:read_next_header
